+intervals. `OutcomeService::captureCheckpoint` validates run identity and any supplied
+source identity, then pins intermediate envelopes to server-owned source/run inputs;
+the final envelope keeps its strict validation. No Python loop, prompt or budget policy
+changes are involved. Area/lead upserts, absolute usage, checkpoint hash/time, a progress
+version and at most 100 public activity entries commit together. Repeated snapshots do
+not duplicate records or usage. Acquisition errors retain the previous valid state and
+never restart the model process. The terminal import marks previously acquired leads
+absent from the final projection `is_current=false`, preserving their history while
+excluding them from findings/counts. Deferred proposals stay separate from admitted
+investigations; active lifecycle states are provisional `running`, not final suspects.
+
+The authenticated SSE endpoint under `projects/{project}/audit-runs/{run}/events`
+publishes database snapshots after version/status changes, with heartbeats and a
+version/status/finish cursor. Reconnect reconstructs current state rather than replaying
+token or tool logs. Overview requests summary-only snapshots; scan detail also receives
+finding summaries and bounded activity. Streams close after 25 seconds or termination;
+the browser reconnects while active and closes on navigation. Deploy behind an HTTP
+server with concurrent workers and unbuffered SSE responses. No stream or page starts
+a scan. Findings resolve evidence on demand against the run's fixed source; report and
+JSON/Markdown exports use persisted product data. A terminal status alone does not make
+a report ready while cleanup/import is unfinished. Failed runs can expose saved
+checkpoints as partial reports; unfinished investigations keep their original verdict
+and are labelled Unfinished rather than assigned a fabricated result.
 
